<title>ITALY: Sorin sells diagnostic interests.</title>
<headline>Sorin sells diagnostic interests.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sorin Biomedica said on Tuesday it signed a contract for the sale of its diagnostic interests and of a 52 percent stake in Incstar Corp to American Standard Cos Inc.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the deal would be completed in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>The statement said that the sale would complete Sorin's divestment of its interests in biochemical reagents which in 1996 accounted for around one quarter of consolidated sales.</p>
<p>Proceeds of more than 300 billion lire from the sale would allow for more aggressive development of the company's artificial organs business which generated around 700 billion lire of sales in 1996.</p>
<p>Some 500 billion lire was accounted for by cardio-vascular organs.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
